        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2089b338-1798-55e6-8f76-9daed4db35e5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Lincoln Neiman, Carrie Marcus Neiman, Herbert Marcus, Minnie Lichtenstein Marcus\n- Companies: A. Harris & Company, Neiman Marcus\n- Places: Chicago, Cleveland, Dallas, Atlanta\n- Topics: marriage, cofounding, sales promotion\n\nFacts:\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman was born on July 4, 1875, in Chicago, Illinois, and he was raised in a Jewish orphanage in Cleveland, Ohio.\n- Carrie Marcus Neiman was born on May 3, 1883, and she later became an American businessperson.\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman met Carrie Marcus Neiman in Dallas, Texas, while both were working at A. Harris & Company.\n- Abraham Lincoln Neiman and Carrie Marcus Neiman married in 1905.\n- After their marriage, Abraham Lincoln Neiman and Carrie Marcus Neiman moved to Atlanta, Georgia, with Herbert Marcus and Minnie Lichtenstein Marcus to do sales promotion work.\n- The Neiman and Marcus families relinquished rights to sales territories in a nascent soft drink concern for $25,000.\n- In 1907, the Neiman and Marcus families used the $25,000 to open Neiman Marcus in Dallas.\n- Carrie Marcus Neiman was one of the cofounders of Neiman Marcus, a luxury department store.\n- Carrie Marcus Neiman died on March 6, 1953.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ddb5c72d-4f89-5e2e-9ca2-0dd32c2ae17b",
        "text": "Page: Abraham Lincoln Neiman. Sentence: Abraham Lincoln \"Al\" Neiman was born on July 4, 1875, in Chicago, Illinois and raised in a Jewish orphanage in Cleveland, Ohio.\nPage: Abraham Lincoln Neiman. Sentence: He met his first wife Carrie Marcus Neiman in Dallas, Texas, while they were working at A. Harris & Company.\nPage: Abraham Lincoln Neiman. Sentence: They married in 1905 and then moved to Atlanta, Georgia, with Carrie's brother Herbert Marcus and sister in law Minnie Lichtenstein Marcus to do sales promotion work.\nPage: Abraham Lincoln Neiman. Sentence: Therefore, they relinquished rights to sales territories in the nascent soft drink concern for $25,000 which the Neiman and Marcus families used to open Neiman Marcus in Dallas in 1907.\nPage: Carrie Marcus Neiman. Sentence: Carrie Marcus Neiman (May 3, 1883 – March 6, 1953) was an American businessperson and one of the cofounders of Neiman Marcus, a luxury department store.",
